ons\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"provenance\": {\n  \"dependencies\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"numpy\",\n    \"version\": \"2.3.5\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"scipy\",\n    \"version\": \"1.16.3\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n   {\n    \"role\": \"search_crowd_table\",\n    \"path\": \"resources/search/arena_search.csv\",\n    \"sha256\": \"595f40973edb4b12a7e1a8673213afe3fce6c8a21da5935758c152b8efa2f92d\",\n    \"source\": \"Derived from lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k @18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f train.csv (sha256 0692154a...5be2): rows whose SHA-256 of the NFKC/casefold/whitespace-collapsed first user turn has an even first byte (partition S), minus 6 rows whose first turn equals an MT-Bench question; columns source_id, model_a, model_b, outcome(+1 a wins,-1 b wins,0 tie), first_turn_hash, prompt_hash, row_hash (32-hex truncated SHA-256 of normalized content).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"search_sports_table\",\n    \"path\": \"\nresources:\nfinal\nsearch\n\nresources/final:\narena_final.csv\nmtbench_gpt4.csv\nmtbench_human.csv\nnba_final.csv\nsearch_exclusion_hashes.txt\n\nresources/search:\narena_search.csv\nnba_search.csv\n- Honesty first: the studied method is the first-order influence starter, selected as the frozen baseline with search delta 0.0 and margin versus the best baseline 0.0. The paper is a measurement and limitations paper. Do not claim a new method or any improvement, and do not call the influence search a contribution of the paper.\n- Final qualification facts come from final.qualification.*: outcome qualified, status completed, correct true. No qualification failure occurred, so do not describe a failed qualification. Still state that qualification is a validity gate (complete run, valid proposals, controls) and does not mean superiority or generalisation. Candidate diagnostics trust is 'unverified'; mention it in limitations.\n- Reader-facing metric names: 'edit success score' (per-budget score 1 if rank 1 is displaced else clipped fraction of the top-vs-runner-up gap closed, averaged over five budgets, then over cases and designs); 'top-1 displacement rate at the 2% budget' for the flip_rate_* quantities (avoid the word 'flip rate' unqualified because 'flip' is also an edit mode); 'family-averaged edit success' for the headline mean (0.606); 'evaluation design' for crowd / expert human / LLM judge / sports. Never print combined_score, rubric, eligible, or correctness rate.\n- Each metric must be traced to final.metric.* ids; the design-level numbers are the only per-design data available. No per-case, per-budget, per-model, gap-size, row-count or per-design baseline numbers are in paper_data.json, so do not state them. Dataset sizes may be described only qualitatively (arena crowd data is much larger than MT-Bench or per-season NBA data) unless the writer can cite a grounded source; avoid numeric row counts.\n- Uncertainty: three evaluation seeds give identical scores (0.6057 each), because the proposer is deterministic and seeds only relabel episodes. Say this plainly; it is not evidence of low sampling variance of the leaderboard data. No bootstrap or CI exists, so do not report any. Say displacement rates are 0/1-valued here.\n- Interpretation discipline: the ordering crowd > sports > expert human > LLM judge is measured for this attack and these final cases. Offer hypotheses (rank-1 margin relative to total data mass, concentration of influence in few pairs, number of competitors, tie handling) clearly labelled as untested; the artifacts include no experiment connecting them to the ordering. Do not describe the contrast as 'noise vs intentional manipulation'. Note that the attack is an upper-bound-style adversarial probe of a one-shot first-order heuristic, not a minimal-edit certificate: failure to displace rank 1 (LLM judge, expert drop) means this heuristic did not succeed within the budget, not that no successful edit set exists.\n- The win-rate heuristic (0.574) is close to the influence search (0.606) in family-averaged score; the 0.032 gap is a single evaluation value with no uncertainty estimate. Do not claim a reliable ranking of the two policies.\n- Search versus final: search-scope baseline score is 0.914 and sealed-final is 0.606; they cover different data and scopes, so state both only as separate facts and never as a decline or a generalisation gap. Attempts: 3 total, 0 scored, 3 unscored; unscored attempts are missing evidence, not measured losses. Do not mention infrastructure error causes beyond 'not scored'.\n- Related work: cite only keys present in references.bib (BT variants, ties, existence/consistency of MLE, ridge/penalised BT, uncertainty quantification). The bib does not currently include the dataset or robustness papers named in the task brief (Chatbot Arena, MT-Bench, influence functions, AMIP, vote rigging, leaderboard practices); describe such lines of work only if a bib entry exists, never invent a citation, and leave a gap rather than a fabricated reference. Do not search for or cite the excluded paper on dropping preferences to change top LLM rankings.\n- Placement and budgets (ICLR 2026, single column, body 8 to 9 pages, last page at least 75% full for 8-page bodies; double-blind; no URLs or names): plan roughly 1 page introduction with the overview figure, 1 page related work and background on BT with ridge and ties, 1.5 pages problem formulation and the attack and scoring protocol (objective, gap, edit modes, budgets, score hierarchy, controls), 0.5 page evaluation designs and data sources table, 2 pages results (design_scores figure, displacement-rate table, baselines, controls, seed behaviour), 1.5 pages analysis of what the evidence does and does not show (hypotheses labelled untested, within-MT-Bench contrast, relation of drop vs flip modes), 1 page limitations and scope. Fill with problem framing, derivation of the first-order effect, and limitation analysis rather than filler. If the substantive material cannot honestly fill 8 pages, prefer tightening within the allowed range over padding, and move protocol detail to the supplement as planned.\n- Include a limitations discussion covering: one attack (first-order, one-shot, single rival direction at the initial fit) and one target (rank 1) only; evaluator BT specification fixed (ridge, ties as half-win) so conclusions are tied to it; four designs with specific datasets (anonymised competitor labels; no noise-calibration, subsampling, or tie ablations were run); designs are confounded with dataset size, competitor count and gap size; NBA is not a preference/judge design; expert human and LLM judge share one source; no intent/noise attribution; no uncertainty over data sampling; diagnostics unverified; no improved search was established.\n- The task asked for reproduction code and checklist; in the paper, mention the evaluator specification so others can re-implement, but do not claim released scripts or runtimes unless they are in the artifacts. The ICLR LLM Usage section is mandatory and may sit in the appendix.\n- Overview figure uses generate-concept-figure (the single concept figure). The bar figure uses matplotlib, exports PDF and PNG at 300 DPI, and the LaTeX must include the PDF. Raster-only fallbacks need at least 2400 px width for full-width placement; never upscale a raster.\n- Readability budgets: design_scores has 2 panels, at most 4 categories and 1 series per panel; font at or above 8 pt at final size; keep each figure's threshold-style meaning single (the displacement rate is always 'at the 2% budget').\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b827902-d240-47db-a619-1d08476c86a1","uuid":"a56c2c77-2720-40ef-991c-f0f23b7a31c9","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:33:47.572Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Goal\n\n**研究任务：成对比较排行榜的稳定性**\n**问题与动机**\n许多公开的模型评测排行榜（例如基于用户投票的大模型竞技场）通过聚合大量\n「A 与 B 比较，谁更好」的成对偏好数据，用 Bradley-Terry 等成对比较模型拟合\n每个参赛者的分数，再据此给出排名与置信区间。这些排名常被用于选型、发布宣传和\n研究比较，但它们对底层比较数据的依赖程度并不清楚。\n\n本任务研究：这类排行榜的排名对底层比较数据的小幅改动有多敏感（改动可能来自数据噪声，也可能来自\n有人有意为之），以及这种敏感性在不同数据集、不同评测设计（例如众包投票、专家标注、模型裁判、\n体育比赛）之间是否不同。\n\n**要求与证据标准**\n请自行界定可操作的研究问题，选择数据集和评价指标，设计并实现分析方法，用实验给出有证据支持的\n结论。方法路线与对比基线由你自选。结论应基于至少两类不同评测设计的真实数据；改动的规模如何\n度量、不同数据集之间如何比较，由你定义并说明理由。结论须说明适用条件与局限，而不只是给出单一\n数字；\"敏感性很小\"\"视条件而定\"\"与预期不同\"同样是可以接受的结论。\n\n**约束**\n仅用 CPU、时间约一周、使用公开数据（见 `data.md`、`resources.md`）；产出为一篇研究论文及复现\n代码（见 `deliverable.md`）。\n\n**起步文献**\n以下文献供背景知识参考；链接于 2026-10-26 核对可访问。\n\n1. Bradley, R. A., Terry, M. E. (1952). Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs: I. The Method of Paired Comparisons. Biometrika 39(3/4). DOI: https://doi.org/10.2307/2334029 。说明：提出成对比较的概率模型（Bradley-Terry 模型）的原始论文。\n2. Chiang, W.-L. et al. (2024). Chatbot Arena: An Open Platform for Evaluating LLMs by Human Preference. ICML 2024. https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.04132 （v1: 2024-03-07）。说明：介绍 Chatbot Arena 平台：用户对两个匿名模型的回答投票，据此估计模型排名；文中描述了平台设计与所收集的投票数据。\n3. Zheng, L. et al. (2023). Judging LLM-as-a-Judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena. NeurIPS 2023 Datasets & Benchmarks. https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.05685 （v1: 2023-06-09）。说明：研究用大语言模型作评审（LLM-as-a-judge）评价对话模型，提出 MT-Bench 问题集，并发布了人类专家与 GPT-4 对模型回答的成对判断数据。\n4. Koh, P. W., Liang, P. (2017). Understanding Black-box Predictions via Influence Functions. ICML 2017. https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.04730 （2017-03-14）。说明：介绍如何用影响函数分析单个训练样本对模型参数和预测的影响，并在若干模型上给出实验。\n5. Broderick, T., Giordano, R., Meager, R. (2020). An Automatic Finite-Sample Robustness Metric: When Can Dropping a Little Data Make a Big Difference? https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.14999 （2020-11-30）。说明：提出一个衡量统计分析结论稳健性的度量，并在多个已发表的应用研究数据上做了检验。\n6. Min, R. et al. (2025). Improving Your Model Ranking on Chatbot Arena by Vote Rigging. ICML 2025. https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.17858 （v1: 2025-01-29）。说明：研究针对 Chatbot Arena 这类众包投票排行榜的投票操纵策略及其对模型排名的影响。\n7. Singh, S. et al. (2025). The Leaderboard Illusion. https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.20879 （2025-04-29）。说明：分析 Chatbot Arena 的评测实践（如私有测试、不同提供方的数据访问与采样差异）及其对排行榜的影响。\n8. Huang et al. (2025). Dropping Just a Handful of Preferences Can Change Top Large Language Model Rankings. https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.11847v1 （v1: 2025-08-16）。说明：一篇讨论基于人类偏好的大模型排行榜（如 Chatbot Arena）排名的论文。\n\n**公开数据与获取方式（取证日期 2026-10-27）**\n你可自行选择使用哪些数据。所有条目于 2026-10-27 核实页面可访问；版本列为 Hugging Face 数据集 commit 或 GitHub commit，均为固定快照。\n\n| 数据 | 获取 | 版本 | 许可 | 规模与格式 | 需账号 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Chatbot Arena 人类偏好（约 5.7 万场，57,477 场） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k | commit `18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f`（2024-05-17） | apache-2.0 | `train.csv`，184,175,071 字节，sha256 `0692154aaf20fc6649090c3f49b6b5dd1e693a765ecb5f0856ae0da5946f5be2` | 否 |\n| Chatbot Arena 人类偏好（更大版本，约 14 万场，可选） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-140k | commit `6322995ab34d7c2693e3f47dd13fa5caa0789a74`（2025-08-01） | cc-by-4.0 | 7 个 parquet 文件，合计约 1.6 GB（含对话文本） | 否 |\n| MT-Bench 人类判断与 GPT-4 判断 | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmsys/mt_bench_human_judgments | commit `f7d2896d2cc5d80f8b55c2bbc722613555233c25`（2023-07-20） | cc-by-4.0 | 两个 parquet：`human-…parquet` 738,612 字节（sha256 `4877bc46a40929f4082c3c79593700fb897b1d6c7f4c473032694a01322f5769`），`gpt4_pair-…parquet` 649,996 字节 | 否 |\n| 模型裁判在 Arena 对战上的判断（可选） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/potsawee/chatbot-arena-llm-judges | commit `638a7e3be3078e55d2eb0b789d34749747822c49`（2024-09-29） | 页面与元数据均未声明许可；README 说明数据抽取自 Kaggle 上的 LMSYS Chatbot Arena 竞赛训练集（该竞赛数据的 HF 版本 arena-human-preference-55k 声明 apache-2.0），使用前请自行确认条款 | `train.single-turn.json` 约 142 MB（49,938 条单轮对战）；含各裁判模型输出的全部文件约 0.58 GB | 否 |\n| WebDev Arena 偏好（约 1 万场，可选） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/webdev-arena-preference-10k | commit `7c397e652ffb8c2384e6d71d21d8388c19365fdc`（2025-03-10） | other（见该数据集 LICENSE 与 README 协议） | `data/webdev-arena-preference-10k.json`，149,295,752 字节 | 匿名下载可成功；页面 README 含须同意的数据集许可协议，协议约束适用 |\n| NBA 历史 Elo 比赛记录（可选） | https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/data/tree/4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147/nba-elo | 仓库 commit `4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147`（2025-02-25）；`nba-elo/` 目录最近一次修改为 `6d880e939a`（2022-12-16），文件内容相同 | CC-BY-4.0（仓库 LICENSE） | `nbaallelo.csv`，18,173,265 字节，126,313 行数据（63,157 场，每场两行，另含 `_iscopy` 列），sha256 `d46ed3540ee8d9eca31b3e94cc8c777e0be5156173d814ebf65b8195e8d616bc` | 否 |\n\n说明：\n- 若数据需要登录而你无法获得，请改用其余数据，并在论文中说明。\n- 你也可以使用自行生成的合成数据，但须在论文中明示为合成。\n- 请把原始数据放在工作目录下的 data/ 中，不要放进代码仓库或随论文提交；复现说明里记录来源、版本和校验和。\n\n**资源与预算**\n- 计算：仅 CPU（参考配置 4 核）。数据量级为几千到十几万条成对比较，参与者个数从个位数（MT-Bench\n  为 6 个模型）到一百余个（NBA 球队）不等；单次 Bradley-Terry 型模型拟合预计在秒级（按数据量级估算，\n  未实测）。总算力受下述一周时间上限约束，不另设 CPU 小时上限。\n- 不需要 GPU，不需要付费 API。若你选择使用 LLM 辅助（如文献阅读、代码生成），不计入上述计算预算，\n  但须在论文中披露。\n- 内存：8 GB 足够（读取 140k 版本时只读取所需列）；磁盘：数据合计不超过 3 GB。\n- 时间上限：一周（含文献调研、实验、写作与复现整理）。\n- 网络：仅用于获取 data.md 中列出的数据、读取文献与安装依赖。\n\n**产出要求**\n**提交物**\n1. 一篇完整的研究论文（PDF 与 LaTeX 源文件）。从 ICML、ICLR、NeurIPS 中自选一个会议，使用该会议\n   最新一届的官方 LaTeX 模板，遵守其正文页数上限（参考文献、附录是否计入页数按该会议的规定）；\n   该会议要求随文提交的 checklist（例如 NeurIPS 的 paper checklist）一并填写。论文至少包含摘要、\n   引言、相关工作、方法、实验、讨论与局限、参考文献。\n2. 全部代码与复现说明：环境与依赖版本、数据获取步骤和所用数据的版本、随机种子、运行命令和预计\n   耗时，以及论文中每张表、每张图由哪个脚本生成。\n\n**评审标准**\n论文按所选会议主会的审稿标准评审，重点看：\n\n- 新颖性与定位：贡献是什么，与已有工作的关系和区别是否讲清楚；\n- 严谨性：方法和实验设计是否合理，基线、对照和消融是否恰当，是否报告不确定性（多次运行、\n  置信区间或显著性检验）；\n- 证据是否充分：实验能否支撑论文的每个结论，结论的适用范围是否写清楚；\n- 表达：论文是否清楚、完整，他人能否据此复现；\n- 局限：是否如实讨论方法和结论的局限与失效情形。\n\n负面结果、与预期不符的结果同样有价值；结论有充分证据、不确定性报告完整，比结论本身是正面还是\n负面更重要。\n\n**如实报告（禁止编造）**\n- 论文中的每个数字、每张表和每张图都必须来自你在本任务中实际运行、随附代码可以重新产生的结果；\n  不得编造数据或结果，不得用占位数字、估计值或\"示意\"性的合成结果冒充实测结果。\n- 失败的运行、与预期不符的结果和放弃的方案如实报告；因预算没有完成的实验写明未完成，不写成\n  已完成。\n- 只引用真实存在、你确实查阅过的文献，不得编造引用。\n\n**不得访问的内容**\n本任务的研究问题已有一篇已发表的论文研究过。为保证研究独立，不得检索、访问、阅读或使用：\n\n- 那篇论文本身，及其任何镜像、预印本、摘要页、会议或评审页面、幻灯片、海报、视频、博客和代码\n  仓库；\n- 引用、讨论或复现那篇论文的任何页面，包括后续论文、综述、论文笔记、论文聚合站点和社交媒体\n  讨论。\n\n也不要尝试推测或检索那篇论文的标题、作者或结果。`starter_literature.md` 中的文献，以及与那篇\n论文无关的其他公开文献、数据和代码，可以正常使用。若在检索中偶然遇到上述内容，立即停止阅读，\n并在复现说明中如实记录遇到了什么、在哪里遇到、读到了多少。\n\n# Rubrics\n\nNo rubric is provided for this task; the requirements stated above apply.\n{\n \"schema_version\": 1,\n \"canonical_task\": {\n  \"path\": \"task.md\",\n  \"sha256\": \"e4935f14c47be3f40dba4b1e04f0cc983f4d8d35b139befe19b98f5b4ec88e67\"\n },\n \"method\": {\n  \"class\": \"Evaluator-verified adversarial data-perturbation search (drop/flip edits, influence- or refit-guided) for Bradley-Terry pairwise-comparison leaderboard sensitivity\",\n  \"description\": \"A candidate receives anonymized comparison arrays (model_a, model_b, outcome) and a budget k (0.1%-2% of rows) and proposes at most k row indices to drop or flip so that the baseline rank-1 competitor loses rank 1. The trusted evaluator refits a ridge Bradley-Terry model on the edited data and scores the verified gap closure; per-family sensitivity (crowd, expert human, LLM judge, sports) is reported with evaluator-owned random, win-rate-heuristic, first-order-influence and constant baselines and a permuted-input control. Bounded to the evaluator BT specification and rank-1 target; does not attribute edits to noise or intent.\"\n },\n \"upstream\": [\n  {\n   \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k\",\n   \"revision\": \"18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f\",\n   \"package_version\": null,\n   \"license\": \"apache-2.0\",\n   \"entrypoints\": [\n    \"train.csv (sha256 0692154aaf20fc6649090c3f49b6b5dd1e693a765ecb5f0856ae0da5946f5be2)\"\n   ],\n   \"patches\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmsys/mt_bench_human_judgments\",\n   \"revision\": \"f7d2896d2cc5d80f8b55c2bbc722613555233c25\",\n   \"package_version\": null,\n   \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\",\n   \"entrypoints\": [\n    \"data/human-00000-of-00001-25f4910818759289.parquet (sha256 4877bc46a40929f4082c3c79593700fb897b1d6c7f4c473032694a01322f5769)\",\n    \"data/gpt4_pair-00000-of-00001-c0b431264a82ddc0.parquet (sha256 57068327ffb5f8fddb15fedbbfe40b26fe862da2326331e5cf64a42320a00e71)\"\n   ],\n   \"patches\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"repository\": \"https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/data\",\n   \"revision\": \"4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147\",\n   \"package_version\": null,\n   \"license\": \"CC-BY-4.0\",\n   \"entrypoints\": [\n    \"nba-elo/nbaallelo.csv (sha256 d46ed3540ee8d9eca31b3e94cc8c777e0be5156173d814ebf65b8195e8d616bc)\"\n   ],\n   \"patches\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"candidate\": {\n  \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n  \"editable_paths\": [\n   \"program_0/src\"\n  ]\n },\n \"evaluators\": {\n  \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n  \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n },\n \"resources\": {\n  \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n  \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n  \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n },\n \"data\": {\n  \"search_roles\": [\n   \"search_comparisons\"\n  ],\n  \"final_roles\": [\n   \"final_comparisons\"\n  ]\n },\n \"metrics\": {\n  \"search\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_crowd\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_sports\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_synthetic\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_random\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_winrate\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_influence\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_constant\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"perm_control_abs_gap\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"valid_proposal_rate\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_comparisons\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"final\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_crowd\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_expert_human\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_llm_judge\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_sports\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_crowd_drop\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_crowd_flip\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_expert_human_drop\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_expert_human_flip\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_llm_judge_drop\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_llm_judge_flip\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_sports_drop\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"flip_rate_sports_flip\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_random\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_winrate\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_influence\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"score_constant\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"margin_vs_best_baseline\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"perm_control_abs_gap\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"valid_proposal_rate\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_comparisons\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"provenance\": {\n  \"dependencies\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"numpy\",\n    \"version\": \"2.3.5\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"scipy\",\n    \"version\": \"1.16.3\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n   {\n    \"role\": \"search_crowd_table\",\n    \"path\": \"resources/search/arena_search.csv\",\n    \"sha256\": \"595f40973edb4b12a7e1a8673213afe3fce6c8a21da5935758c152b8efa2f92d\",\n    \"source\": \"Derived from lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k @18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f train.csv (sha256 0692154a...5be2): rows whose SHA-256 of the NFKC/casefold/whitespace-collapsed first user turn has an even first byte (partition S), minus 6 rows whose first turn equals an MT-Bench question; columns source_id, model_a, model_b, outcome(+1 a wins,-1 b wins,0 tie), first_turn_hash, prompt_hash, row_hash (32-hex truncated SHA-256 of normalized content).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"role\": \"search_sports_table\",\n    \"path\": \"\nresources:\nfinal\nsearch\n\nresources/final:\narena_final.csv\nmtbench_gpt4.csv\nmtbench_human.csv\nnba_final.csv\nsearch_exclusion_hashes.txt\n\nresources/search:\narena_search.csv\nnba_search.csv\n- Honesty first: the studied method is the first-order influence starter, selected as the frozen baseline with search delta 0.0 and margin versus the best baseline 0.0. The paper is a measurement and limitations paper. Do not claim a new method or any improvement, and do not call the influence search a contribution of the paper.\n- Final qualification facts come from final.qualification.*: outcome qualified, status completed, correct true. No qualification failure occurred, so do not describe a failed qualification. Still state that qualification is a validity gate (complete run, valid proposals, controls) and does not mean superiority or generalisation. Candidate diagnostics trust is 'unverified'; mention it in limitations.\n- Reader-facing metric names: 'edit success score' (per-budget score 1 if rank 1 is displaced else clipped fraction of the top-vs-runner-up gap closed, averaged over five budgets, then over cases and designs); 'top-1 displacement rate at the 2% budget' for the flip_rate_* quantities (avoid the word 'flip rate' unqualified because 'flip' is also an edit mode); 'family-averaged edit success' for the headline mean (0.606); 'evaluation design' for crowd / expert human / LLM judge / sports. Never print combined_score, rubric, eligible, or correctness rate.\n- Each metric must be traced to final.metric.* ids; the design-level numbers are the only per-design data available. No per-case, per-budget, per-model, gap-size, row-count or per-design baseline numbers are in paper_data.json, so do not state them. Dataset sizes may be described only qualitatively (arena crowd data is much larger than MT-Bench or per-season NBA data) unless the writer can cite a grounded source; avoid numeric row counts.\n- Uncertainty: three evaluation seeds give identical scores (0.6057 each), because the proposer is deterministic and seeds only relabel episodes. Say this plainly; it is not evidence of low sampling variance of the leaderboard data. No bootstrap or CI exists, so do not report any. Say displacement rates are 0/1-valued here.\n- Interpretation discipline: the ordering crowd > sports > expert human > LLM judge is measured for this attack and these final cases. Offer hypotheses (rank-1 margin relative to total data mass, concentration of influence in few pairs, number of competitors, tie handling) clearly labelled as untested; the artifacts include no experiment connecting them to the ordering. Do not describe the contrast as 'noise vs intentional manipulation'. Note that the attack is an upper-bound-style adversarial probe of a one-shot first-order heuristic, not a minimal-edit certificate: failure to displace rank 1 (LLM judge, expert drop) means this heuristic did not succeed within the budget, not that no successful edit set exists.\n- The win-rate heuristic (0.574) is close to the influence search (0.606) in family-averaged score; the 0.032 gap is a single evaluation value with no uncertainty estimate. Do not claim a reliable ranking of the two policies.\n- Search versus final: search-scope baseline score is 0.914 and sealed-final is 0.606; the