and one target (rank 1) only; evaluator BT specification fixed (ridge, ties as half-win) so conclusions are tied to it; four designs with specific datasets (anonymised competitor labels; no noise-calibration, subsampling, or tie ablations were run); designs are confounded with dataset size, competitor count and gap size; NBA is not a preference/judge design; expert human and LLM judge share one source; no intent/noise attribution; no uncertainty over data sampling; diagnostics unverified; no improved search was established.\n- The task asked for reproduction code and checklist; in the paper, mention the evaluator specification so others can re-implement, but do not claim released scripts or runtimes unless they are in the artifacts. The ICLR LLM Usage section is mandatory and may sit in the appendix.\n- Overview figure uses generate-concept-figure (the single concept figure). The bar figure uses matplotlib, exports PDF and PNG at 300 DPI, and the LaTeX must include the PDF. Raster-only fallbacks need at least 2400 px width for full-width placement; never upscale a raster.\n- Readability budgets: design_scores has 2 panels, at most 4 categories and 1 series per panel; font at or above 8 pt at final size; keep each figure's threshold-style meaning single (the displacement rate is always 'at the 2% budget').","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace/paper","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
