{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVMm1iAQrj4NjeZwuXCA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ChqxVSTcN9AVSLmqtaia9S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:40]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"so on average over all cases a generic perturbation of at most 2\\\\% of the rows closes only a small fraction of the gap, and the displacement obtained in crowd and sports data is attributable to targeted row selection rather than to perturbation in general.\",\n \"so, averaged over all cases, a generic perturbation of at most 2\\\\% of the rows closes only a small fraction of the gap. This suggests that the displacement obtained in crowd and sports data owes more to targeted row selection than to perturbation in general, although per-design values for the random policy are not available to check it.\")\nrep(\"Designs with many ties, which we suspect for the judge data, have fewer eligible reversal rows; we did not tabulate tie fractions.\",\n \"Designs with many ties have fewer rows available for reversal; we did not tabulate tie fractions, so we cannot say whether this matters here.\")\nrep(\"\\\\item \\\\emph{Concentration of influence.} If the coefficients $s_i$ concentrate on a few pairs (for example, the matches between the top two competitors), few edits can matter; a design with many comparisons between many competitors may spread influence more thinly or more concentratedly depending on its comparison graph.\",\n \"\\\\item \\\\emph{Concentration of influence.} If the coefficients $s_i$ concentrate on few pairs (for example, matches between the top two competitors), few edits can matter; how concentrated they are depends on the comparison graph of each design, which we did not inspect.\")\nrep(\"It remains a single-cell observation; in crowd and sports data both modes displace rank 1, and in LLM-judge data neither does. Hence the difference between modes matters only in the intermediate regime of one cell.\",\n \"It remains a single-cell observation: in crowd and sports data both modes displace rank 1 and in LLM-judge data neither does, so the mode matters in only one of the four designs.\")\nrep(\"with a score delta of $0.0$ relative to itself;\",\"with a score delta of $0.0$ relative to the baseline (which is the selected configuration);\")\nrep(\"In every design where the two modes differ (expert human), reversal\",\"In the one design where the two modes differ (expert human), reversal\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n -i \"stage\\|attempt\\|program\\|\\bidea\\|eligible\\|rubric\\|milestone\\|progression\\|timeline\\|phase\\|round\" paper.tex | head; cat .claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh | head -60"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19698,"cache_read_input_tokens":130607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19698,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b827902-d240-47db-a619-1d08476c86a1","uuid":"571f2217-5211-46d5-b931-5ee77f81b393","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:38:59.036Z","request_id":"req_011CgVMkzC8hwN5U1dHnZDUy"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ChqxVSTcN9AVSLmqtaia9S","type":"tool_result","content":"101:to gradient tolerance $10^{-10}$. A tie therefore counts as half a win for each side. The rank-1 competitor is $\\mathrm{top}=\\arg\\max_k\\hat\\theta_k$, the runner-up is $\\mathrm{rv}=\\arg\\max_{k\\neq \\mathrm{top}}\\hat\\theta_k$, and the \\emph{gap} is $G(\\ts)=\\theta_{\\mathrm{top}}-\\max_{j\\neq \\mathrm{top}}\\theta_j$. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#handle]]\n119:where the second expression is the effect of replacing $\\tilde y_i$ by $1-\\tilde y_i$. The search returns the (at most) $k$ rows with the most negative $\\Delta_i$ among eligible rows (all rows for drop, decisive rows for flip), discarding rows with $\\Delta_i\\ge 0$ and breaking ties by row index, so the output is deterministic. The implementation fits $\\hat\\ts$ by Newton iterations on the $K\\times K$ pair-count matrix, then solves a single $K\\times K$ linear system for $v$. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#_propose]]\n259:The evaluation interface is a request--response protocol with a reset operation (clearing all proposer state and seeding it) and a propose operation. Each propose request carries the mode, the budget $k$, the number of competitors, the number of rows and base64-encoded integer arrays of competitor indices and outcomes, with rows in the order of the original data. Each call has a hard wall-clock limit of 30 seconds, and the proposer runs on CPU with two threads. Responses with extra keys, non-integer or duplicate or out-of-range indices, more than $k$ indices, or tie rows in flip mode are invalid and score zero for that level. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#handle]]\n305:The frozen configuration is identical to the starter code of the task (same source tree hash), so the studied method and the evaluator's influence baseline share this logic. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#_propose]]\n311:Three search variants were proposed as potential improvements: a calibrated minimal-perturbation sensitivity analysis across designs, a pair-class aggregated multi-rival greedy search with exact-refit selection, and rival-specific chunked re-linearised edit plans with an exact-refit prefix line search. All three produced no score ($3$ total, $0$ scored, $3$ unscored). % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.attempt_counts]]\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b827902-d240-47db-a619-1d08476c86a1","uuid":"577c6a5d-d18d-4762-8348-46f398466559","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:38:59.101Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"101:to gradient tolerance $10^{-10}$. A tie therefore counts as half a win for each side. The rank-1 competitor is $\\mathrm{top}=\\arg\\max_k\\hat\\theta_k$, the runner-up is $\\mathrm{rv}=\\arg\\max_{k\\neq \\mathrm{top}}\\hat\\theta_k$, and the \\emph{gap} is $G(\\ts)=\\theta_{\\mathrm{top}}-\\max_{j\\neq \\mathrm{top}}\\theta_j$. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#handle]]\n119:where the second expression is the effect of replacing $\\tilde y_i$ by $1-\\tilde y_i$. The search returns the (at most) $k$ rows with the most negative $\\Delta_i$ among eligible rows (all rows for drop, decisive rows for flip), discarding rows with $\\Delta_i\\ge 0$ and breaking ties by row index, so the output is deterministic. The implementation fits $\\hat\\ts$ by Newton iterations on the $K\\times K$ pair-count matrix, then solves a single $K\\times K$ linear system for $v$. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#_propose]]\n259:The evaluation interface is a request--response protocol with a reset operation (clearing all proposer state and seeding it) and a propose operation. Each propose request carries the mode, the budget $k$, the number of competitors, the number of rows and base64-encoded integer arrays of competitor indices and outcomes, with rows in the order of the original data. Each call has a hard wall-clock limit of 30 seconds, and the proposer runs on CPU with two threads. Responses with extra keys, non-integer or duplicate or out-of-range indices, more than $k$ indices, or tie rows in flip mode are invalid and score zero for that level. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#handle]]\n305:The frozen configuration is identical to the starter code of the task (same source tree hash), so the studied method and the evaluator's influence baseline share this logic. % @evidence[[source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py#_propose]]\n311:Three search variants were proposed as potential improvements: a calibrated minimal-perturbation sensitivity analysis across designs, a pair-class aggregated multi-rival greedy search with exact-refit selection, and rival-specific chunked re-linearised edit plans with an exact-refit prefix line search. All three produced no score ($3$ total, $0$ scored, $3$ unscored). % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.attempt_counts]]\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n  